# fixture: withholding-exceeds-paycheck  (adversarial)
#
# payroll withholding larger than the paycheck it comes out of. A 401(k)
# that closes mid-plan books its whole balance as income on day 1, before
# payroll runs, and payroll sizes the household withholding from that month
# x12, so the close month asks one $6,000 paycheck for a six-figure
# withholding. A paycheck pays taxes first and deferrals from what is left,
# so it withholds everything after FICA, the IRA deferral gets nothing, and
# the rest of the estimate goes to the true-ups as unpaid. Booked as
# withheld instead, it would count as paid and be refunded in cash. The
# deferral is load-bearing: it is what a paycheck short of its taxes gives
# up, so a pipeline that paid deferrals before taxes would move this
# baseline. So is the salary running past the close: end it first and there
# is nothing to over-withhold. Every rate is zero, so the money can be
# followed by hand. deferred-close-distribution reaches the same month with
# growth and no deferral; tests/payroll-withholding-conservation.mjs holds
# the conservation law.

